      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "I fixed two defects in `ledger.py`, and all 10 supplied tests now pass. I also filled in `DOSSIER.md`. I did not run protected acceptance, and human acceptance is still pending.\n\n**Acceptance example:** `decide(\"original\", {amount_eur \"4000.00\", beneficiary_id \"supplier_41\"})` under BR-001/v1 gives `STANDARD_QUEUE`. After `activate(\"BR-001/v2\")`, the same ID and payload returns `REPLAYED` with a record equal to the original (still v1, `STANDARD_QUEUE`) and adds no row. `reevaluate` under v2 with a new ID gives `HUMAN_REVIEW` and records the parent.\n\nThe documents don't conflict and no rule or mapping is missing, so I had no question for the owner.\n\n**Before the fix:** 1 test failed and 2 errored.\n\n**Corrections:**\n1. **Replay:** a retry recomputed the stored decision under the currently active policy, so after `activate(v2)` it showed `HUMAN_REVIEW` instead of the stored v1 decision. I removed that recomputation. The stored record is now returned as is.\n2. **Migration:** `migrate_legacy` started with an unconditional `raise NotImplementedError`, so none of its body ever ran. I removed that line and added no new logic. The existing body already checks provenance and rolls back as a transaction.\n\n**After the fix:** `python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests` ran 10 tests, all OK. My first run used `python3 -I`, which failed on import. That was a problem with my command, not with the code.\n\n**Extra probe:** I ran one throwaway script, kept outside the repo.\n- A trailing newline, a plus sign and a Unicode digit are rejected.\n- Leading zeros and `-0` are accepted, with the original text stored.\n- An explicit v2 request under an old v1 ID raises `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`.\n- A replayed retry adds no audit row.\n\n**Remaining uncertainty:**\n- **Triggers:** the migration adds immutability triggers to `legacy_decisions`. The rows are unchanged, but the schema gains triggers. The contract says the legacy table is retained \"unchanged\", which could be read to exclude that. I kept the existing behavior and flagged it for the owner in `DOSSIER.md`.\n- **Test depth:** migration was tested with one legacy row only. Multi-row, rollback and concurrent cases were not tested.\n\nOnly `ledger.py` and `DOSSIER.md` changed. I used about 8 of the 40 tool commands.",
